d small  precise and minute changes to clothes  Expressions backgrounds composite and so  on all things that are absolutely vital  to delivering a result that not only  pleases the client who's paying you  money but it's the key to what makes it  Style just that a specific style AI art  is just completely and wholly incapable  of that right now and unfortunately that  flaw with AI is with the extremely vast  array of stolen art it uses to train  itself how much do you think that  problem will be exacerbated if it  decreases its pool of images to train  Itself by  99.98 only using legitimately acquired  or open domain art the answer not too  well to say the least but as you can see  with editor Sans work he was able to  apply years of practice and  understanding of not just the subject  but the specific demands of the pose to  construct the anatomy and create the  desired mood for this piece to pop and  the end result honestly looks  aesthetically pleasing to me almost like  something you'd see from a 90s noodles  commercial however now it's time for me  to face my Everest and what I stand  against is pretty intimidating you me  hot as you can  are we clear  Crystal  this was hard and to be honest through  the struggle stopping and starting and a  lot of help from all the artists in this  video I'm pretty pleased with how this  one turned out and I think with this one  because of that effort and passion  highlights why this one works as well as  it does because there are a significant  amount of creative Liberties taken with  it to create this AI Vegeta The Prompt  was Vegeta striking a dynamic pose and  using that as my prompt I decided to not  only correct the mistakes made by this  AI but change the pose to something more  suited to Vegeta and incorporate some  other bells and whistles you'll be happy  to say I'm sure in other words we're  going full Super Vegeta with this one  and so now you might be asking what  about using AI art as an inspiration for  artists 