gely and Implement artwork that  resonated with me what I felt like  drawing using effects work and shading  that I felt at work and reminded me of  one of my favorite artists yuya  takahashi's work while also implementing  some of my own stylistic Works into the  mix creating a brand new piece and  hopefully you think it looks cool which  brings us thankfully to our last drawing  of the video and it comes by way of AI  trash here we have I think Gohan riding  a bike and believe it or not this was  the best of the bunch that we generated  for this particular image complete with  cousin thing from The Adams Family on  the left handlebar in this video we've  taken a rather negative albeit  principled approach against AI generated  art but that's also not to say that AI  art has no place at all far from it it's  clearly already become this incredible  tool that's taken the Internet by storm  and so if nothing else I posit that it  has a true use and that purpose is  larger than one everyone at this point  has largely seen it is an exceptionally  fun toy to experiment with we've  established that using it for any form  of profit or claim is inherently immoral  as it is and we've also covered that it  lacks the depth and specificity to  replace actual illustrators concept  artists and the like in any real Prof  professional setting but look across the  internet and you'll also see what  99.99999 of the people that have been  using it have been doing and you will  see exactly how it shines it is a very  fun pretty powerful toy you're certainly  not going to get the same level of craft  thought and creativity that you would  otherwise get from a real life artist  after commissioning them but you know  what you can do generate an image of  Adele eating a burger the wrong way in  10 seconds you can generate an image of  Shrek playing basketball on the moon an  image of Gohan riding a sick motorcycle  along a dirt road with a new outfit and  when you think about it that's an 